From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: cv18xx: power up the PLL before changing its rate

Accessing a powered-down PLL stalls the SoC on the register write. The
assigned-clock path runs before the consumer enables its clock
(of_clk_set_defaults runs before probe), so programming cam0pll for the
UART hung the EVB before any further output. Clear the power-down bit
and settle briefly before touching the PLL registers.

--- a/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-pll.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/limits.h>
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
@@ -360,6 +361,16 @@
 	if (!fpll_is_factional_mode(pll))
 		return ipll_set_rate(hw, rate, parent_rate);
 
+	/*
+	 * A powered-down PLL stalls the SoC on a register access. The
+	 * assigned-clock path runs before the consumer enables its clock
+	 * (of_clk_set_defaults runs before probe), which hung the EVB.
+	 */
+	if (!pll_is_enable(hw)) {
+		pll_enable(hw);
+		udelay(20);
+	}
+
 	fpll_find_rate(pll, &pll->pll_limit[2], parent_rate,
 		       &rate, &detected, &detected_ssc);
 	pll_get_mode_ctrl(PLL_GET_DIV_SEL(detected),

